1
00:00:14,030 --> 00:00:18,101
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:19,402 --> 00:00:22,739
Oh, yeah!  I'm going to
start the Laser Channel.

3
00:00:22,739 --> 00:00:25,575
All lasers, all the time.

4
00:00:25,575 --> 00:00:27,310
Actually, I guess it's not all the time.

5
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:28,845
That's a problem, isn't it?

6
00:00:28,845 --> 00:00:31,481
I need a way for this thing
to fire continuously.

7
00:00:31,481 --> 00:00:34,017
And it's not doing much good
pointed at this wall.

8
00:00:34,017 --> 00:00:35,485
I need to reflect it somewhere.

9
00:00:36,152 --> 00:00:37,320
What's that say?

10
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:39,856
"Do Not Obstruct Laser Shield"

11
00:00:39,856 --> 00:00:41,691
Big letters, too.

12
00:00:41,691 --> 00:00:44,594
It looks almost asking for
someone to obstruct it, isn't it?

13
00:00:44,594 --> 00:00:46,696
I don't care for your rules.

14
00:00:46,696 --> 00:00:49,032
Now I want to see what
happens when it gets obstructed.

15
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,701
There, that should do it.

16
00:00:51,701 --> 00:00:54,437
I've never used a laser this big.
I don't know what'll happen.

17
00:00:54,437 --> 00:00:57,006
If it starts bouncing everywhere,
I'll just run out of the room.

18
00:01:00,343 --> 00:01:02,145
(chuckling) Aw-aw-awesome!

19
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,746
It's burning it up.

20
00:01:04,881 --> 00:01:05,715
[explosion]

21
00:01:05,715 --> 00:01:07,450
OH!

22
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:09,986
That's even better than I expected!

23
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,554
Look at that sucker!

24
00:01:11,554 --> 00:01:13,957
Aw! Oh no!

25
00:01:13,957 --> 00:01:16,726
Don't stop; let's keep
this laser party going!

26
00:01:16,726 --> 00:01:19,095
Get a disco ball and some music in here.

27
00:01:19,095 --> 00:01:20,797
Maybe clear out the bodies.

28
00:01:20,797 --> 00:01:24,467
Hell, shoot the laser at the disco ball
and set this whole room on fire.

29
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,637
Hm, this material is slower going.

30
00:01:27,637 --> 00:01:30,573
It might take me too long to
carve a tunnel out of here this way.

31
00:01:30,573 --> 00:01:33,576
Even though that would be
totally awesome!

32
00:01:33,576 --> 00:01:34,577
Hm.

33
00:01:34,577 --> 00:01:36,479
Wait, where does this room even go?

34
00:01:36,946 --> 00:01:38,448
It goes down.

35
00:01:38,448 --> 00:01:39,582
Can't say I like that.

36
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:42,752
But this whole building's
a dead end except for the ceiling.

37
00:01:43,653 --> 00:01:47,123
I guess I could push that crate
all the way downstairs to get out.

38
00:01:47,123 --> 00:01:48,458
I mean, I don't have any duct tape,

39
00:01:48,458 --> 00:01:49,926
otherwise, I'd tape down that button,

40
00:01:49,926 --> 00:01:53,029
take a nap, and let the laser
burn a hole out of here.

41
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:56,099
But this crate must weigh at
least 200 pounds.

42
00:01:56,099 --> 00:01:58,668
Damn, and I'll have to push it
up those other stairs,

43
00:01:58,668 --> 00:02:01,671
or else go the long way
around with that ramp.

44
00:02:01,671 --> 00:02:03,973
Screw that, I'll check out
this room first.

45
00:02:04,574 --> 00:02:05,508
And, hey, if I

46
00:02:05,508 --> 00:02:06,576
(gasps)

47
00:02:06,576 --> 00:02:08,778
If I slip and crack my skull,

48
00:02:08,778 --> 00:02:11,848
then, at least I know
this was the wrong...

49
00:02:11,848 --> 00:02:12,315
...decision.

50
00:02:13,416 --> 00:02:17,320
God, no matter how much I try, I
can never ignore gravity.

51
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:19,255
It's just always there.

52
00:02:19,255 --> 00:02:20,757
Talk about oppression.

53
00:02:20,757 --> 00:02:21,424
It's-- (screams)

54
00:02:21,958 --> 00:02:23,159
You never get a break.

55
00:02:24,327 --> 00:02:24,694
Yee...!

56
00:02:25,328 --> 00:02:28,631
Unless you're...
completely underwater.

57
00:02:28,631 --> 00:02:30,066
But then, you can't breathe.

58
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:30,900
So, what the hell?

59
00:02:31,334 --> 00:02:33,970
This is an awfully big ceiling.

60
00:02:33,970 --> 00:02:36,539
Maybe they used to have a
giant trampoline in here.

61
00:02:36,539 --> 00:02:37,407
I would.

62
00:02:37,874 --> 00:02:38,808
Oh, oh!

63
00:02:38,808 --> 00:02:40,977
SCIENTIST #1: A scientist! Thank God!

64
00:02:40,977 --> 00:02:44,247
SCIENTIST #1: Get us out of here
before those military drones figure out

65
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:44,881
SCIENTIST #1: where we're hiding.

66
00:02:44,881 --> 00:02:45,348
Okay...

67
00:02:45,348 --> 00:02:47,784
SCIENTIST #2: We all have
retinal scanner access.

68
00:02:47,784 --> 00:02:50,820
SCIENTIST #2: Escort us to the lobby
and we can get out of the lab.

69
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:51,354
Well, I--

70
00:02:51,354 --> 00:02:51,621
SCIENTIST #3: You'll have to shut down

71
00:02:51,621 --> 00:02:53,656
JESUS CHRIST!
SCIENTIST #3: the surgical unit, first.

72
00:02:53,656 --> 00:02:55,191
TRYING TO FLANK ME!
SCIENTIST #3: Peters switched it on

73
00:02:55,191 --> 00:02:56,726
SCIENTIST #3: but I'm afraid he
never made it back.

74
00:02:56,726 --> 00:02:58,261
Okay, everybody, shut up!

75
00:02:58,261 --> 00:02:59,562
I need to think.

76
00:02:59,562 --> 00:03:02,565
Okay, I won't be killing you
because you told me exactly

77
00:03:02,565 --> 00:03:03,199
what I wanted to hear.

78
00:03:03,199 --> 00:03:04,300
SCIENTIST #1: It appears the
containment system has

79
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:06,836
SCIENTIST #1: completely failed.
Hey, what did I just say?!

80
00:03:06,836 --> 00:03:08,805
I can still change my mind!

81
00:03:08,805 --> 00:03:11,641
There's enough in this clip for
every one of you.

82
00:03:11,641 --> 00:03:13,643
Okay, let's do the Get Outside thing.

83
00:03:13,643 --> 00:03:14,744
You!  Come with me!

84
00:03:14,744 --> 00:03:17,847
SCIENTIST #1: With my brains and
your brawn, we'll make an excellent team.

85
00:03:17,847 --> 00:03:21,117
Oh! So, you think YOU'RE the
brains of this operation, huh?

86
00:03:21,117 --> 00:03:21,684
SCIENTIST #1: I'll wait.

87
00:03:21,684 --> 00:03:24,020
SCIENTIST #2: Fascinating!
God damned RIGHT you will!

88
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:26,589
SCIENTIST #2: I never suspected
such things could be.

89
00:03:26,589 --> 00:03:28,124
Okay, Dopey, YOU come with me.

90
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:28,991
SCIENTIST #2: All right.

91
00:03:30,093 --> 00:03:32,495
Okay, now this slicer is
kind of dangerous.

92
00:03:32,495 --> 00:03:35,031
You ought to know; you designed it.

93
00:03:35,031 --> 00:03:36,099
Now, just take your time.

94
00:03:36,099 --> 00:03:38,101
It's only a concentric circle pattern.

95
00:03:38,101 --> 00:03:38,568
All you have to--

96
00:03:38,568 --> 00:03:40,403
[squish]

97
00:03:40,403 --> 00:03:42,138
What the fuck?

98
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:44,474
Looks like I picked the wrong man for the job!

99
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:46,109
Jesus Christ!

100
00:03:47,844 --> 00:03:50,546
This just looks bad
for everyone involved.

101
00:03:51,414 --> 00:03:52,148
God.

102
00:03:52,715 --> 00:03:54,617
Oh, yeah, better make sure
the door opens.

103
00:03:54,617 --> 00:03:56,819
That would really cap
things off it if doesn't.

104
00:03:57,687 --> 00:03:58,488
Good.

105
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:01,624
If this was locked, it would be
a massacre trying to get this crew

106
00:04:01,624 --> 00:04:03,593
to climb up the pipes I came
down on.

107
00:04:03,593 --> 00:04:05,161
Okay, people, time for Plan B.

108
00:04:05,161 --> 00:04:07,897
SCIENTIST #3: Who is responsible
for this mess?

109
00:04:07,897 --> 00:04:09,265
I don't like how you're looking at me.

110
00:04:09,265 --> 00:04:10,500
Are we going to have a problem here?

111
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,100
SCIENTIST #3: Let's go!

112
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,869
Good.  Okay, I guess, you too.

113
00:04:12,869 --> 00:04:14,704
SCIENTIST #1: I certainly hope
you know what you're doing.

114
00:04:14,704 --> 00:04:17,173
That's it!  I've had enough
lip from you!  You stay!

115
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:18,341
SCIENTIST #1: I'm...slowing you down, am I?

116
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:20,543
No, you're pissing me off is
what you're doing!

117
00:04:20,543 --> 00:04:22,879
What I SHOULD do is to turn
that cheese slicer back on

118
00:04:22,879 --> 00:04:25,648
and let you form your own
escape plan, brainiac!

119
00:04:25,648 --> 00:04:26,916
Like I need your help.

120
00:04:26,916 --> 00:04:31,387
SCIENTIST #3: I hope those people in the
Lambda Lab can get this under control.

121
00:04:31,387 --> 00:04:35,358
Well, if they're anything like Poindexter
back there, I think we're on our own.

122
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:36,459
Oh, now watch out here.

123
00:04:36,459 --> 00:04:38,561
These aliens ended up on display somehow.

124
00:04:38,561 --> 00:04:40,830
I hate these things and you should, too.

125
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:43,199
And don't tap on the glass.
They hate that.

126
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:44,367
See, watch this.

127
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,134
[glass shatters, alarm sounds]

128
00:04:45,134 --> 00:04:45,568
Shit!

129
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:48,938
I DIDN'T MEAN TO DO THAT!

130
00:04:49,472 --> 00:04:52,842
Scientist #3: I seem to be
wounded but I can keep going.

131
00:04:52,842 --> 00:04:55,578
Wow, you're pretty chill about all this.

132
00:04:55,578 --> 00:04:57,747
Kind of unnaturally so.

133
00:04:57,747 --> 00:04:59,382
I guess you're autistic.

134
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:00,383
Great.

135
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:01,484
Well, follow me.

136
00:05:04,654 --> 00:05:06,122
SCIENTIST #3: Well, there
goes our grant money.

137
00:05:06,122 --> 00:05:06,756
God!

138
00:05:08,958 --> 00:05:09,959
Well, I don't know what to say.

139
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:13,696
I don't know why all the glass in the
hallway shattered at the same time.

140
00:05:13,696 --> 00:05:15,965
Or why you would design
something like that.

141
00:05:15,965 --> 00:05:18,401
I also think the sirens are
really unnecessary,

142
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,670
though that would make a pretty
good alarm clock sound.

143
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:23,306
You'd wake up and think there's
a bombing raid going on.

144
00:05:23,306 --> 00:05:24,707
Well, here's the scanner--

145
00:05:24,707 --> 00:05:25,241
AGH!

146
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:26,943
I SAID NO TAGBACKS!

147
00:05:26,943 --> 00:05:28,244
WHAT THE HELL?!

148
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:30,046
Christ, I thought I got this guy.

149
00:05:30,046 --> 00:05:33,182
SCIENTIST #3: Well, I'll let you out, but
I'm warning you, it's hell out there!

150
00:05:33,182 --> 00:05:34,150
Oh, unlike here, right?

151
00:05:34,150 --> 00:05:35,985
SCIENTIST #3: It's completely
under military control.

152
00:05:35,985 --> 00:05:38,788
SCIENTIST #3: You'll have to sneak and
fight your way from one end to the other.

153
00:05:38,788 --> 00:05:42,525
SCIENTIST #3: And I don't expect you'll
meet many of our peers along the way.

154
00:05:42,525 --> 00:05:45,895
SCIENTIST #3: But, if you DO survive,
and somehow make it across the base,

155
00:05:45,895 --> 00:05:47,463
SCIENTIST #3: you'll end up at
the Lambda Complex,

156
00:05:47,463 --> 00:05:48,531
No, I'm going to leave!

157
00:05:48,531 --> 00:05:50,333
SCIENTIST #3: where the rest of
the Science Team has taken shelter.

158
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:52,168
SCIENTIST #3: I wouldn't
venture there myself,

159
00:05:52,168 --> 00:05:53,269
SCIENTIST #3: but I will let them know

160
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:55,371
SCIENTIST #3: that you are coming.
Dude, you've been shot!

161
00:05:55,371 --> 00:05:58,374
You should find some gauze; make
sure the bleeding's under control.

162
00:05:58,374 --> 00:06:00,009
No, don't walk on it!

163
00:06:00,009 --> 00:06:03,279
I've taken some shots, too, but
I'm in plated body armor.

164
00:06:03,279 --> 00:06:04,714
Big difference.

165
00:06:04,714 --> 00:06:06,549
Big, big difference.

166
00:06:06,549 --> 00:06:09,919
Stop walking on it and
go find some disinfectant!

167
00:06:09,919 --> 00:06:11,387
That's irony for you.

168
00:06:11,387 --> 00:06:14,924
He's the only person in this building
who's been even remotely helpful.

169
00:06:14,924 --> 00:06:17,393
So, naturally, he's going
to get himself killed.

170
00:06:19,095 --> 00:06:22,932
Oh, my God!  I'm outside at last!

171
00:06:22,932 --> 00:06:24,133
Again!

172
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:24,567
Agh!

173
00:06:26,836 --> 00:06:30,106
This endless desert isn't big
enough for the both of us.

174
00:06:30,106 --> 00:06:31,941
Huh, it's kind of hot out here.

175
00:06:31,941 --> 00:06:34,410
But, I still don't want to go
inside ever again.

176
00:06:34,410 --> 00:06:36,379
Whoa, it looks like somebody
lost an argument.

177
00:06:36,379 --> 00:06:37,580
[turret whines, beeps]

178
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:40,116
Oh, there's that noise.

179
00:06:40,116 --> 00:06:41,417
Is that real?

180
00:06:41,417 --> 00:06:43,119
I don't like that noise.

181
00:06:43,119 --> 00:06:44,620
Okay, I saw something.

182
00:06:45,855 --> 00:06:47,590
Not a weathervane!
Not a weathervane!

183
00:06:47,590 --> 00:06:50,126
It looks like an anemometer,
but it is not!

184
00:06:50,126 --> 00:06:53,696
Anemometers don't fire bullets,
not even the expensive ones.

185
00:06:53,696 --> 00:06:54,964
Or, I don't think they do.

186
00:06:54,964 --> 00:06:57,733
If they do, meteorologists are
more hardcore than I thought.

187
00:06:59,068 --> 00:07:01,070
Well, I don't know.  Maybe.

188
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:02,805
They chase tornadoes and crap.

189
00:07:02,805 --> 00:07:05,207
Maybe this is what happens when
they get better funding.

190
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,743
STOP BEEPING!

191
00:07:09,812 --> 00:07:12,615
No more measuring wind speed for you!

192
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:15,418
So, maybe this is the
Meteorology Department.

193
00:07:15,418 --> 00:07:17,553
That would explain all the skylights.

194
00:07:17,553 --> 00:07:21,157
Doesn't really explain the lasers
or slicing machine, though.

195
00:07:21,157 --> 00:07:22,158
What's this?

196
00:07:22,525 --> 00:07:24,727
Or the crates of explosives.

197
00:07:24,727 --> 00:07:27,163
Actually, I don't think this
belongs to the Science Team.

198
00:07:27,163 --> 00:07:28,431
We make our own.

199
00:07:28,431 --> 00:07:30,733
Okay, don't shoot this.

200
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:37,540
But, yeah, I could see meteorologists
taking things up a notch.

201
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,275
Like they normally release
weather balloons

202
00:07:39,275 --> 00:07:42,645
then just count on people to be
nice and mail them back when they land.

203
00:07:42,645 --> 00:07:45,381
Instead, they could deploy
motion-sensor turret guns on landing,

204
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:48,751
send out a locator signal and
shoot anyone that got too close.

205
00:07:48,751 --> 00:07:50,252
They'd get their data then.

206
00:07:50,853 --> 00:07:53,389
Now, is there's another turret
gun waiting for me?

207
00:07:53,389 --> 00:07:54,790
Oh!

208
00:07:55,491 --> 00:07:58,761
Somebody did not hear me
through their helmet.

209
00:07:58,761 --> 00:08:02,665
You know, the Art of War talks
about terrains, spies, the use of fire,

210
00:08:02,665 --> 00:08:05,234
but, I'd bet if Sun Tzu had
access to satchel charges,

211
00:08:05,234 --> 00:08:07,670
he would've authored a whole new
section on them alone.

212
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:09,138
Wow, they didn't notice that?

213
00:08:09,138 --> 00:08:10,873
They must be listening to the radio.

214
00:08:10,873 --> 00:08:12,108
I'm going to change the station.

215
00:08:12,108 --> 00:08:15,344
[BOOM!]

216
00:08:15,344 --> 00:08:18,147
Well, all in all, it's not
such a bad way to go.

217
00:08:18,147 --> 00:08:21,050
Confusion for half a second, then death.

218
00:08:21,851 --> 00:08:23,419
I would feel bad about this,

219
00:08:23,419 --> 00:08:27,957
but morality is for people who don't have
other people trying to kill them every five minutes.

220
00:08:27,957 --> 00:08:31,794
I mean, this isn't like a basketball
game where I'm winning over and over.

221
00:08:31,794 --> 00:08:34,597
"C'mon!  Let us win just once!"

222
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:37,600
"C'mon, Gordon, let us kill you just once!"

223
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,403
HECU: Check your zone.
Yeah...

224
00:08:40,403 --> 00:08:42,705
HECU: Sir, I hear something.

225
00:08:42,705 --> 00:08:44,974
[overlapping HECU chatter]
Jesus.

226
00:08:44,974 --> 00:08:45,608
HECU: SHIT!

227
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:49,545
Whoo-hoo-hoo!
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

228
00:08:49,545 --> 00:08:50,546
I hope you're not upset about--

229
00:08:53,549 --> 00:08:54,150
Never mind.

230
00:08:54,917 --> 00:08:56,886
Whuh-hoo, well, that wakes me up.

231
00:08:56,886 --> 00:09:01,357
Wow, I almost feel like I don't
even need more stimulants today.

232
00:09:01,357 --> 00:09:02,858
I guess I need some downers.

233
00:09:03,526 --> 00:09:05,728
[chopper hum]

234
00:09:05,728 --> 00:09:08,097
Wow, I didn't know we had a dam.

235
00:09:08,097 --> 00:09:09,932
[explosions]

236
00:09:09,932 --> 00:09:11,167
HAD a dam...

237
00:09:11,167 --> 00:09:14,370
[mortar fire]

238
00:09:14,370 --> 00:09:15,805
[explosions]

239
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:20,009
I...don't...think my suit can
stop mortar shells.

240
00:09:21,677 --> 00:09:25,281
Oh, a helicopter with rockets.

241
00:09:25,281 --> 00:09:30,586
So, that means climbing the rocks
out of here isn't really an option.

242
00:09:30,586 --> 00:09:31,821
Well....

243
00:09:32,288 --> 00:09:33,622
Shit!

244
00:09:36,125 --> 00:09:40,129
I'm embarrassed that I've been outwitted
by a squad of soldiers with mortar shells

245
00:09:40,129 --> 00:09:43,499
and a helicopter with rocket
missiles in a boxed-in canyon,

246
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:45,567
but, here I am.

